            "summary": "This document is a Combined Adverse Event / Product Complaint Report concerning a 29-year-old male patient who experienced adverse reactions after using Cortivex Cream. The cream was applied topically twice daily from July 20 to July 21, 2026. The patient developed skin inflammation and blistering at the site of application within hours of the first use, and these symptoms are ongoing at the time of the report.\n\nThe report is filed by T. Tomlin, a pharmacist from the USA. There is a mention of a potential product defect, as the batch lot number B4471 is associated with visible discoloration and an unusual odor in the cream. No photos are provided to support the observations.\n\nGiven the reported skin reactions and the potential defect of the product, this document is relevant to patient safety and quality complaint reviews. It highlights serious concerns regarding the product's integrity and its effects on a patient, warranting further investigation into the safety and quality of Cortivex Cream."
